                  "fullEntry":  "The Mimir are the mask-wearers of the Frostwood canopy, and they have never shown their faces to outsiders. They were made by Sereth, the dead creator-deity of perfection and form, whose shame at his imperfect creation drove him to hide his people from the world itself. Sereth gave them the power to shift their shapes \u2014 to be anything except what they were. But the fog that saved the Reach from freezing also devours memory. After generations in the mist, a Mimir can forget their own face. So they carve masks from heartwood or storm-glass, and the mask becomes the only thing holding them together \u2014 a blank canvas for an identity they can no longer remember.\n\nThe Masked rule the canopy-holds as aristocrats. The Woven keep watch from the high aeries, maintaining a living mask-craft tradition through storm-glass forging. The Unwoven, born without masks or the ability to shapeshift, drift the valley floor carrying cracked heirlooms no one remembers how to repair. At the heart of Masked territory lies Mirror Mere, a lake so still it returns a Mimir\u0027s true face even when they can no longer recall it.\n\nThe original art of carving masks was lost when the inquisitors burned the birthing chambers during the Mimir Purge. The Woven\u0027s living craft preserves fragments of the old knowledge, but the technique that created the first masks died with Sereth. The Hunters pay fortunes for Mimir masks on the black market. And every year, the fog grows a little thicker.",
