    "wyrd":  {
                 "id":  "wyrd",
                 "term":  "Wyrd",
                 "type":  "concept",
                 "region":  "sundale",
                 "summary":  "The raw substance of unmaking that bled through Sol\u0027s broken seal. It takes the shape of whatever a population fears most.",
                 "fullEntry":  "The Wyrd is not magic. It is the raw, entropic substance of unmaking, the blood of Keth-Amar that bled through the fractures in Sol\u0027s binding seal when the Breach shattered the vault. Where magic builds, the Wyrd unbuilds. Where magic names, the Wyrd unnames.\n\nThe Wyrd grows in four tiers, each more dangerous than the last. At the first and most passive level, Wyrd-Taint, the corruption seeps into the land itself: blackened flora, wrong-colored water, crops that taste of ash. A region exposed long enough develops Wyrd-taint in the soil before any creature manifests. At the second tier, Wyrd-Wisp, enough shared fear within a tainted region condenses the Wyrd into visible phenomena \u2014 moving shadows, whispers in wind, shapes at the edge of vision. Not yet animated, but felt. At the third tier, Wyrd-Spawn, a fear with sufficient psychic weight is given a body. These are the monsters born from what the local people dread most: the Gref, the Gambrel, the Stel. At the fourth and highest tier, Wyrd-Channel, a Wyrd-Spawn that has grown powerful enough becomes a conduit for Keth-Amar\u0027s direct attention \u2014 boss-tier entities through which the Sun-Eater can perceive, whisper, and direct. Most Wyrd-Spawns never reach this level. Those that do are the Wyrd-priests, Monolith guardians, and cult leaders who have fully surrendered.\n\nThe Wyrd answers to mortal consciousness, and what it answers to first is fear. Keth-Amar does not personally create most Wyrd-Spawns. It seeds the soil (Wyrd-Taint) and waits for fear to do the rest. The Wyrd is Keth-Amar\u0027s agriculture.\n\nWyrd concentration was first confined to the Emberspire caldera. Through the Contraction phase of the early and middle Diming centuries, the seal-cracks widened under geothermal pressure and Wyrd-miasma spread across the continent. In the Squeeze that followed, the mid-to-late Diming, Wyrd-density reached epidemic levels. Entire settlements were abandoned to Wyrd-manifestations. The Inquisitor order was founded specifically to hunt and sever Wyrd-creatures, and the cold-iron blade became the only reliable answer.\n\nThe Wyrd is not diminishing. It is accelerating.\n\nStand in the wrong grove at the wrong hour and the Wyrd will learn what you fear. The Inquisitors can teach you to cut it. They cannot teach you to unlearn it. The next shape it wears may already be yours.",
