                                "fullEntry":  "The Watcher in the Mist is one face of a single entity: the Keeper of the Last Threshold, known as Morvane to the Neth of the Bryngloom and as the Watcher to the peoples of the Frostwood Reach. It is the boundary between life and death, memory and oblivion. It does not serve Aethil and is not answerable to Keth-Amar. It reached House Viridane in the moonlit groves during their flight south \u2014 not chosen, but answering at the last possible moment because total imbalance is the one thing it cannot permit. Older than Keth-Amar\u0027s hunger and more patient, it offered the fleeing family a counter-bargain: protection from the Sun-Eater\u0027s sight in exchange for a permanent bond to the groves. The Watcher is not the dead moon\u0027s dreaming consciousness \u2014 the moon is a separate dormant star (Selunis) \u2014 but the Watcher is the entity that keeps it dormant, and the Watcher\u0027s fracturing under Keth-Amar\u0027s pressure is what allows the moon to stir. It hid House Morrath\u0027s false shard \u2014 the false shard fabricated to cover Viridane\u0027s vacant seat \u2014 in a pocket of forgotten memory at the moment of the Breach, and sheltered Viridane\u0027s true seventh fragment in the moonlit groves with the Briaran. The erasure worked too well; now even Morvane cannot find the exact grove where the true fragment sleeps. Walk the moonlit groves with thorns on your arms and you may hear what House Viridane heard; the Watcher is still there, still patient, still remembering what everyone else has forgotten.",
