                      "term":  "The Dead Moon (Selunis)",
                      "type":  "entity",
                      "region":  "frostwood-reach",
                      "summary":  "A dormant star \u2014 an ancient, sleeping deity whose shattered fragments became the lunar parasites.",
                      "fullEntry":  "The dead moon is not a moon, and it was never a moon. It is a dormant star \u2014 an ancient, sleeping deity named Selunis, unconscious for eons. Its awareness withdrew so deep that only the shell remained. What sent it into this slumber is unknown; it was not Keth-Amar, who arrived far later, tracking the Astril refugees from Lumia, and found a corpse-star already waiting.\n\nWhen it shattered \u2014 whether by age, internal pressure, or the same cosmic hunger that stalks Sol \u2014 its fragments fell across the Frostwood Reach. The fae of the moonlit groves gathered the largest pieces and nurtured them. From those fragments emerged the lunar parasites: void-adapted organisms that feed on memory, sensation, and vitality. They are the only living traces of the sleeping star\u0027s inner ecology.\n\nSome call the moon an \"egg,\" and they are closer to the truth than they know: a deity slumbers within the dormant star, and one day the shell must crack. The lunar parasites \u2014 void-adapted organisms that feed on memory, sensation, and vitality \u2014 are the living traces of that sleeper\u0027s inner ecology, siblings born of the same dormant star and now communicating across hosts. The old belief that it was merely a dead celestial body was the prevailing scholarly consensus; the truth is stranger and older than any corpse, and the deity within is the reason the Astril still sing to Selunis, trying to wake it gently rather than let it hatch in catastrophe.\n\nLook up on a clear night in the Frostwood Reach and you\u0027ll see where the dead moon used to hang, a dark socket in a sky that has no stars. The fragments are below. The parasites are awake. And the elder parasites, bonded to the first Lunarchs, are beginning to synchronize toward something no living scholar understands.",
